  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Lilagenin and the NQO1 protein, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with NQO1. Lilagenin is linked to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-10, which is a target of several compounds, including 2-Hydroxy-3,5,5-trimethylcyclohex-2-ene-1,4-dione, [(2S)-3-hydroxy-1-(7-methoxy-2-oxochromen-8-yl)-3-methylbutan-2-yl] 3-methylbutanoate, and 2-Amino-5-(2-(4-(hydroxymethyl)phenyl)hydrazinyl)-5-oxopentanoic acid. These compounds all have a common target of NQO1, indicating a possible pathway through which Lilagenin may influence NQO1 activity. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, but the exact mechanism by which Lilagenin interacts with NQO1 remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential regulatory or inhibitory role for Lilagenin in NQO1, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
